# Retire policy 2026-11-20: still in production in 2026 with no announced end; retire dates commented out. Revisit when an end is announced.
# Porsche Macan Electric five-door SUV, 2024 onwards.
#
# The electric Macan: the PPE-platform SUV with the closed nose, the
# four-point light signature, the sloping rear roofline and the full-width
# tail lamp. It is a different car from the 2014-23 petrol Macan, which is not
# represented in this object.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porsche_Macan
#
# Dimensions 4.784 x 1.938 x 1.622 m, wheelbase 2.893 m.
#
# Shape reference: the pack's images show a UK car in side, front and rear
# views; the side view governs the sloping roof and the short overhangs.
#
# Colours: grade (b), a franchised UK Porsche Centre's reproduction of the
# maker's UK option list: White, Jet Black, Gentian Blue and Volcano Grey.
# Weights 12, 10, 10, 8, total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 230 km/h. Comfort 95/473, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 95: a quiet,
# spacious electric SUV. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2024 intro, retire dates commented out (still in production in 2026).
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/porsche-macan-electric.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/porsche-macan-electric.dae. References:
# citycars/references/porsche-macan-electric/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the electric XAB only. The flank is estimated from a
# show car about 35-40 degrees off the side, and the road-car fascia is used.
# Turbo roof rails are omitted. The split headlamps, the diffuser and the
# full-width tail bar are simplified, with no lettering in the bar.


obj=citycar
name=PorscheMacanElectric(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=2024
intro_month=1
#retire_year=2051
#retire_month=6
speed=230
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=473

